      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00155_p38_b3",
      "text": "[2025] develop distributionally robust regret formulations in modern statistical and learning\nsettings. Our paper imports that line of work into RLHF and shows that the regret\nbenchmark becomes especially natural once reward uncertainty, rather than transition\nuncertainty, is the main source of misspecification.\n",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        253.96,
        523.66,
        319.61
